{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan","id":1465021,"title":"So, what's the plan?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-23T11:31:54-07:00","id":1465021,"title":"So, what's the plan?","content":"For a long time, I've been trying to answer the question as to why I prefer playing with the technocracy and not the council. I found many reasons, but there's one in particular I feel strongly about, and I wanted to share it with you. (Sarcastic and exaggerated dialogue follows)<br /> <br /> <i>Me: &quot;So hey council, what's the plan?&quot;<br /> <br /> Council: &quot;To allow all paradigms to coexist in harmony.&quot;<br /> <br /> Me: &quot;That's a goal, not a plan.&quot;<br /> <br /> Council: &quot;Well, you know, we fight the technocracy to free the masses from...&quot;<br /> <br /> Me: &quot;No I don't know, and that's another goal, what's the actual plan? How are you actually going to achieve it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Council: &quot;We follow the guidance of the arch...o no wait, the avatar storm. Anyway, I meant, the new council will follow a more modern approach, that's for sure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Me: &quot;Sigh...approach to what?&quot;<br /> <br /> Council: &quot;The ascension war.&quot;<br /> <br /> Me: &quot;For the love of...can you give me a straight answer? What are the details? What are the steps?&quot;<br /> <br /> Council: &quot;We do the same thing we have been doing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Me: &quot;So, making it up as we go?&quot;<br /> <br /> Council: &quot;It's not like that...&quot;<br /> <br /> Me: &quot;Suuuuure...by the way, what will the world look like if we achieve victory?&quot;<br /> <br /> Council: &quot;Eh...really cool? Maybe?&quot;<br /> <br /> Me: &quot;I give up...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Here's the thing, the technocracy HAS a plan, an actual strategy with a timetable, phases, and a clear vision of where they are going. Sure, it can be, and has been, a deeply flawed plan, one that has hurt and keeps hurting a lot of people, but you can see the road ahead and an image of that ideal future in series like Star Trek.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Council doesn't have, as far as I can tell, a clear long-term plan and of course no concrete image for what the future they are fighting for looks like. All they have are generic goals and the fact that they don't want the technocracy's vision for the future. Survival and preservation are valid goals, but there has to be something than living in the past,<b> I refuse to believe that the council and traditions can't evolve and offer a unifying vision without loosing their souls. </b><br /> <br /> When I play with the technocracy, I truly feel like I'm part of something bigger that is working towards something. When I play with the Council, I always feel like I'm in a giant ship where every sailor is doing whatever they want and only work together to prevent the ship from sinking.<br /> <br /> Now, perhaps my perception is flawed, and maybe we'll get something more concrete with guide to traditions. In any case, I just wanted to know if you feel the same way, and if that's the case, how do you handle it. I don't think the Council's needs plan a like the technocracy, but I feel they would be more attractive if they had a cleared strategy and vision of the future.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your answers.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 10-23-2021, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T12:25:49-07:00","id":1465024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan#post1465021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a long time, I've been trying to answer the question as to why I prefer playing with the technocracy and not the council. I found many reasons, but there's one in particular I feel strongly about, and I wanted to share it with you.<br /> <br /> <i>So hey council, what's the plan?<br /> <br /> To allow all paradigms to coexist in harmony.<br /> <br /> That's a goal, not a plan.<br /> <br /> Well, you know, we fight the technocracy to free the masses from...<br /> <br /> No I don't know, and that's another goal, what's the actual plan? How are you actually going to achieve it?<br /> <br /> We follow the guidance of the arch...o no wait, the avatar storm. Anyway, I meant, the new council will follow a more modern approach, that's for sure.<br /> <br /> Sigh...approach to what?<br /> <br /> The ascension war.<br /> <br /> For the love of...can you give me a straight answer? What are the details? What are the steps?<br /> <br /> We do the same thing we have been doing.<br /> <br /> So making it up as we go?<br /> <br /> It's not like that...<br /> <br /> Suuuuure...by the way, what will the world look like if we achieve victory?<br /> <br /> Eh...really cool? Maybe?<br /> <br /> I give up...</i><br /> <br /> Here's the thing, the technocracy HAS a plan, an actual strategy with a timetable, phases, and a clear vision of where they are going. Sure, it can be, and has been, a deeply flawed plan, but you can see the road ahead and an image of that ideal future in series like Star Trek.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Council doesn't have, as far as I can tell, a clear long-term plan and of course no concrete image for what the future they are fighting for looks like. All they have are generic goals and the fact that they don't want the technocracy's vision for the future.<br /> <br /> When I play with the technocracy I truly feel like I'm part of something bigger that is working towards something. When I play with the Council, I always feel like I'm in a giant ship where every sailor is doing whatever they want and only work together to prevent the ship from sinking.<br /> <br /> Now, perhaps my perception is flawed, and maybe we'll get something more concrete with guide to traditions. In any case, I just wanted to know if you feel the same way, and if that's the case, how do you handle it. I don't think the Council's needs plan a like the technocracy, but I feel they would be more attractive if they had a cleared strategy and vision of the future.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The plan is:<br /> <br /> * Organized all mages who aren't Technocrats [changed to all non-Union mages including some Technocrats]<br /> * Fortify their Horizon Realms against invasion<br /> * Fight the Union on the beaches and never surrender<br /> * Help Sleepers awaken<br /> * Protect against the Technocracy's persecution of their belief in the consensus<br /> <br /> They've been on the backfoot for 600 years but here's the thing. THEY'RE NOT LOSING.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy has not gotten any closer to destroying the Traditions than they were in the Mythic Age and the One knows how many thousands of Unionists have died and how much of their resources is being wasted on the Ascension War that they keep fighting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T13:38:23-07:00","id":1465033,"title":"","content":"The difference is the kind of goal. The Council don't have or need a unified vision of the world they want. Only the Technocracy have that. The problem is that the Union's plan includes eliminating everyone else in the game.<br /> <br /> If you can't feel that preservation is a valid goal in itself, you sure can't feel attracted to any other faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T14:18:59-07:00","id":1465044,"title":"","content":"Before all of this gets requoted over and over, can I possibly impose with a suggestion?... Editing OP to add some dialogue tags? This is going to be an interesting post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T14:45:43-07:00","id":1465045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan#post1465021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, the Council doesn't have, as far as I can tell, a clear long-term plan and of course no concrete image for what the future they are fighting for looks like. All they have are generic goals and the fact that they don't want the technocracy's vision for the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do have a concrete image for what the future they're fighting for looks like: Horizon. They constructed an entire Umbral Realm that's meant to inspire their members as to what a world under the Traditions would be. I'm not sure you get more concrete than that; yes Revised offed it in the metaplot, but it was a thing.<br /> <br /> And as noted, &quot;survive the Technocracy&quot; is a pretty important goal when the Technocracy is trying to eliminate all non-Union mages. The Traditions started as an alliance of mages for mutual self defense. It's the core of everything they're about because it's what banded them together in the first place. NATO, as it stands now, is a lot more than just a mutual defense pact... but that's still the core of why NATO exists and what bind it together. Countries join NATO because they want to be defended from external threats; even if those have changed over the years. While there are people that question if NATO is needed in the current time, it's not criticized for a lack of specific and clear long term plans or goals beside facilitate it's founding purpose of mutual defense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T14:58:32-07:00","id":1465047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465033#post1465033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is the kind of goal. <b>The Council don't have or need a unified vision of the world they want. </b>Only the Technocracy have that. The problem is that the Union's plan includes eliminating everyone else in the game.<br /> <br /> If you can't feel that preservation is a valid goal in itself, you sure can't feel attracted to any other faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they do.<br /> <br /> Everyone can do whatever kind of magic they want. The goal is freedom to pursue Ascension on your own terms. If they wanted to make a paradigm that suppressed other peoples then they wouldn't be the Traditions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T15:24:11-07:00","id":1465049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465033#post1465033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is the kind of goal. The Council don't have or need a unified vision of the world they want. Only the Technocracy have that. The problem is that the Union's plan includes eliminating everyone else in the game.<br /> <br /> If you can't feel that preservation is a valid goal in itself, you sure can't feel attracted to any other faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Preservation and survival are perfectly valid goals, and the if the Council and Traditions prefer the status Quo then that's their choice. My issue (which is entirely personal, I don't expect, or need, the setting to change to accommodate my preferences) isn't with those goals, my issue comes when that's all there is. I see the value of preserving the wisdom of the past. Thing is, I need something else, something to look forward to, and I don't feel like the Council offers that to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 10-23-2021, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T15:39:44-07:00","id":1465051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465045#post1465045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do have a concrete image for what the future they're fighting for looks like: Horizon. They constructed an entire Umbral Realm that's meant to inspire their members as to what a world under the Traditions would be. I'm not sure you get more concrete than that; yes Revised offed it in the metaplot, but it was a thing.<br /> <br /> And as noted, &quot;survive the Technocracy&quot; is a pretty important goal when the Technocracy is trying to eliminate all non-Union mages. The Traditions started as an alliance of mages for mutual self defense. It's the core of everything they're about because it's what banded them together in the first place. NATO, as it stands now, is a lot more than just a mutual defense pact... but that's still the core of why NATO exists and what bind it together. Countries join NATO because they want to be defended from external threats; even if those have changed over the years. While there are people that question if NATO is needed in the current time, it's not criticized for a lack of specific and clear long term plans or goals beside facilitate it's founding purpose of mutual defense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Horizon is a beautiful vision, but the impression I got (which could be wrong) is that Horizon was something that happened out of convenience, a headquarters to coordinate their efforts against the technocracy. It wasn't an intentional creation to show a vision of the future, but a fortress that expanded as needed and then collapsed due to betrayal (if you follow metaplot). That's not quite the inspiring unifying image I had in mind. <br /> <br /> Again, survival by itself is not an invalid goal, if the Council wants to remain a purely defensive pact then that's their choice. I'm just saying that for me, personally, that's not enough and that's why I have a hard time identifying with the Council. It's a personal preference, it doesn't make the Council less valid as an organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T16:13:37-07:00","id":1465055,"title":"","content":"I'm really not sure what to say if you're going to reject Horizon as a concrete image for the future the Traditions are fighting for.<br /> <br /> What's the point of the thread if the platonic ideal of the Tradition's mutual philosophy isn't good enough to say that yes, there are more than a defensive pact,and that yes, they have a clear vision? You're not going to get affirmation of &quot;the Traditions aren't fun to play if they lack a vision for the future,&quot; while we have the ability to point to what their vision for the future is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T16:24:48-07:00","id":1465058,"title":"","content":"They Traditions fight the war in fairly conventional ways. They engage and destroy technocratic units in the field, fortify/defend their strong points and subtley influence the sleepers to keep there ways alive.<br /> In terms of ascension a unified theory isn't really required since their ascension are individualistic. If the union lost tomorrow they'd simply pursue the distinct approaches without obstruction<br /> <br /> I would also note the ascension war is in fact a 3 way struggle not a two way one.....and the 3rd faction prove that you can work quite effectively independant of one another without the benefit of a big map. Since its suggested they're winning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-23-2021, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T17:35:42-07:00","id":1465068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465058#post1465058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They Traditions fight the war in fairly conventional ways. They engage and destroy technocratic units in the field, fortify/defend their strong points and subtley influence the sleepers to keep there ways alive.<br /> In terms of ascension a unified theory isn't really required since their ascension are individualistic. If the union lost tomorrow they'd simply pursue the distinct approaches without obstruction<br /> <br /> I would also note the ascension war is in fact a 3 way struggle not a two way one.....and the 3rd faction prove that you can work quite effectively independant of one another without the benefit of a big map. Since its suggested they're winning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's a 5 way struggle.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi's statement, &quot;Nope. It's gotta go&quot; is a valid goal with an end.<br /> <br /> Marauders go, &quot;Fuck you. I got mine.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T17:44:02-07:00","id":1465070,"title":"","content":"I think it's okay for a discussion to evolve out of one's personal preferences and head-cannon as a player, but I suspect that you are searching for a reason to play the Traditions just to get some varied play experience. I would not enjoy playing the Technocracy as written, for one reason: Room 101. I wouldn't want to storytell a Technocratic-Union-as-written campaign, because I would be faced with imposing Room 101 on imaginative, rebellious players, which gets into issues of player agency. <br /> <br /> If you enjoy being in lockstep with the Union's stated goals and following orders, then you see the glass half full where the Technocracy are concerned. A way of seeing the glass half full with Traditions is that <i>You</i> can be the Tradition Mage who pulls it all together. You can be the visionary leader who points to the distance, saying, &quot;Follow me to...(use your imagination)&quot;.<br /> <br /> The M20 Character sheet lists: Name, Player, Chronicle, <i>Nature, Demeanor, Essence</i>, Affiliation, Sect, Concept, in that order for a reason. If you are substituting the Technocracy's well defined Timetable for in-depth freeform Seekings, you may be missing out on the opportunity to play in a faction that does not punish deviance from party line with torture and Conditioning. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T18:25:04-07:00","id":1465076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465068#post1465068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it's a 5 way struggle.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi's statement, &quot;Nope. It's gotta go&quot; is a valid goal with an end.<br /> <br /> Marauders go, &quot;Fuck you. I got mine.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Well the 3rd faction is the Nephandi. The closest I've seen to an approximate mission statement is that time I watched a Serbian film, geno cyber and a couple of gasper noe's 'charming' films. What they stand for can't really be defined by words, definition is afterall a child of stasis and dynamism.<br /> Man....the nephandi are awesome bad guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-23-2021, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T18:42:42-07:00","id":1465078,"title":"","content":"There are also the Disparates, who as of the Alliance have as their mission statement \u201cf*** the Nephandi!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T19:56:02-07:00","id":1465087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465078#post1465078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also the Disparates, who as of the Alliance have as their mission statement \u201cf*** the Nephandi!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the mages who go, &quot;I don't care who runs the Consensus. I just want to make lead into gold in my basement.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which was always an idea that was underdeveloped.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T20:32:19-07:00","id":1465089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465070#post1465070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's okay for a discussion to evolve out of one's personal preferences and head-cannon as a player, but I suspect that you are searching for a reason to play the Traditions just to get some varied play experience. I would not enjoy playing the Technocracy as written, for one reason: Room 101. I wouldn't want to storytell a Technocratic-Union-as-written campaign, because I would be faced with imposing Room 101 on imaginative, rebellious players, which gets into issues of player agency.<br /> <br /> If you enjoy being in lockstep with the Union's stated goals and following orders, then you see the glass half full where the Technocracy are concerned. A way of seeing the glass half full with Traditions is that <i>You</i> can be the Tradition Mage who pulls it all together. You can be the visionary leader who points to the distance, saying, &quot;Follow me to...(use your imagination)&quot;.<br /> <br /> The M20 Character sheet lists: Name, Player, Chronicle, <i>Nature, Demeanor, Essence</i>, Affiliation, Sect, Concept, in that order for a reason. If you are substituting the Technocracy's well defined Timetable for in-depth freeform Seekings, you may be missing out on the opportunity to play in a faction that does not punish deviance from party line with torture and Conditioning.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I do understand where you're coming from, I think you're being a bit too rigid here. Yes, Room 101 exists. But they don't send every troublemaker there. It's reserved for the worst offenders, renegades and traitors. Nor does the Technocracy punish innovative and imaginative agents. They will punish those that are dangerously reckless or regularly disobedient but then so would any organization. And even then, Room 101 and the severe punishments are only for those morons that don't seem to get the memo that being a reckless jackass is a bad thing. Again, like any other organization would.<br /> <br /> If a ST of a Technocrat game is threatening PCs with Room 101 for attempting stray from their rails, that's a problem with the ST. Though if a PC is behaving badly, threatening them with Room 101 is valid.<br /> <br /> And Technocrats (as well as other Technomancers) do have Seekings, they just perceive and understand them differently from Mages. Just as Mages from different Traditions will perceive their own Seekings differently from those other Traditions. If they didn't, they wouldn't be able to advance their Enlightenment as other Willworkers do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T21:32:02-07:00","id":1465092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465089#post1465089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do understand where you're coming from, I think you're being a bit too rigid here. Yes, Room 101 exists. But they don't send every troublemaker there. It's reserved for the worst offenders, renegades and traitors. Nor does the Technocracy punish innovative and imaginative agents. They will punish those that are dangerously reckless or regularly disobedient but then so would any organization. And even then, Room 101 and the severe punishments are only for those morons that don't seem to get the memo that being a reckless jackass is a bad thing. Again, like any other organization would.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;dangerously reckless&quot; could just be an inventor whose idea threatens the Timetable. He pursues the tinkering despite being told not to, because his Avatar is threatening to leave if he doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465089#post1465089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a ST of a Technocrat game is threatening PCs with Room 101 for attempting stray from their rails, that's a problem with the ST. Though if a PC is behaving badly, threatening them with Room 101 is valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is one way to suborn someone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465089#post1465089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Technocrats (as well as other Technomancers) do have Seekings, they just perceive and understand them differently from Mages. Just as Mages from different Traditions will perceive their own Seekings differently from those other Traditions. If they didn't, they wouldn't be able to advance their Enlightenment as other Willworkers do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware that Technomancers have Seekings and they can be as profound as those of Tradition Mages. I just think the authoritarian nature of the Technocracy means there will be inevitable conflicts between what a character's Avatar and rank-superior want them to do, often enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T06:40:48-07:00","id":1465131,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26467_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26467\" data-vbnamecard=\"26467\">HorizonParty2021</a>, the point is that the possibility of abuse doesn't mean abuse happens, or that it happens with the frequency you seem to expect. I've enjoyed playing characters with a long history with Room 101, but also enjoyed games where it is used sparingly, as the last resort for agents whose indiscipline have been costing lives time and again.<br /> <br /> Both readings are Union as written. Even because on big institutions a lot of things happen at middle management, so there is no mandatory reading of the institutional rules out or in character. At least not mandatory in a way that can be reliably enforced.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2964_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2964\" data-vbnamecard=\"2964\">Firanai</a>, the Traditions are a defense alliance. They are working toward a greater vision: a world where you can follow your path for Enlightenment without a self-righteous jerk hunting you just out of spite for your personal world view. This is a vision in itself. Also they have individual Traditions and subdivisions carrying on with particular propositions in a way the Conventions can't, as defending diversity of ideas includes, by definition, that you'll have this diversity of ideas to follow or dispute.<br /> <br /> If you don't like it is ok. But in that case you must reframe your reasoning, because we already presented plans, vision, representations, strategy, context, and it so happens that you don't like them, which is very different from them not existing or being ill defined. As you put it in the OP, this is not the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T09:59:34-07:00","id":1465152,"title":"","content":"You all have given me plenty of ideas and perspectives to work with. That said, in order to expand this discussion a bit more and give people more things to work with, I would like us to ignore my personal preferences and hear about your mage's personal take on the ascension war, their plan if you would prefer (if they even have one, the ascension war can be ignored) Perhaps it could be something as simple as this: be the change you want to see in the world, so what does your mage want to see in the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:22:37-07:00","id":1465154,"title":"","content":"I ended up getting back to this a wee bit late, but I do have one other suggestion to offer. The Traditions are not like the Technocratic Union, where all of the Conventions are at least nominally on board with one big Plan for all of them. The Traditions don't have A Plan, they have Nine Plans, one for each Tradition. The Traditions as a collective exist to facilitate each of the individual Traditions pursuing their own agendas, cooperating and protecting each other, and arbitrating disputes (ideally, at least). Most of the plans of the Traditions as a whole will simply be the result of negotiating the best way to advance the common interests of the separate Traditions. If you want a deeper idea of &quot;What is the game plan for the Traditions,&quot; you would probably have to study each Tradition individually rather than try and find a big answer that covers everything.<br /> <br /> I haven't done a ton of digging into the individual Traditions, but one example might be the Virtual Adepts' focus on the Digital Web and Reality 2.0. That's *their* Plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:24:41-07:00","id":1465155,"title":"","content":"Made a new thread for my Union: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465158-union-games-how-dark-to-make-the-technocracy-around-you\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...acy-around-you</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-24-2021, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:25:50-07:00","id":1465157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465154#post1465154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ended up getting back to this a wee bit late, but I do have one other suggestion to offer. The Traditions are not like the Technocratic Union, where all of the Conventions are at least nominally on board with one big Plan for all of them. The Traditions don't have A Plan, they have Nine Plans, one for each Tradition. The Traditions as a collective exist to facilitate each of the individual Traditions pursuing their own agendas, cooperating and protecting each other, and arbitrating disputes (ideally, at least). Most of the plans of the Traditions as a whole will simply be the result of negotiating the best way to advance the common interests of the separate Traditions. If you want a deeper idea of &quot;What is the game plan for the Traditions,&quot; you would probably have to study each Tradition individually rather than try and find a big answer that covers everything.<br /> <br /> I haven't done a ton of digging into the individual Traditions, but one example might be the Virtual Adepts' focus on the Digital Web and Reality 2.0. That's *their* Plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a statement but I don't think its actually the case. The Traditions don't think their plans are contradictory, which is something a lot of players (and to be fair, a lot of Traditionalists) reject.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:36:01-07:00","id":1465161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465157#post1465157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a statement but I don't think its actually the case. The Traditions don't think their plans are contradictory, which is something a lot of players (and to be fair, a lot of Traditionalists) reject.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said their plans were contradictory. I think the points made above about Horizon demonstrate that. But I do think each Tradition, deep down, thinks their Plan is the best Plan. And I think that kind of just comes with the territory of Mages and their strong beliefs/hubris.<br /> <br /> Using my previous example, I don't think that the majority of Dreamspeakers, Hermetics, or Verbena care the tiniest bit about creating the Virtual Adepts' Reality 2.0; there's probably a minority of tech-mages among the Hermetics or urban shaman Dreamspeakers, but mostly they have their own business to attend to. Conversely, the Virtual Adepts won't be helping the other Traditions bring their big plans to fruition beyond individual favors or basic assistance grounded on their mutual interests, quid pro quo or individual acts of generosity. They won't force anyone to join Reality 2.0, but they deep down think that everyone will eventually, acknowledging their paradigm as the best or truest one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T18:22:58-07:00","id":1465228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1465021-so-what-s-the-plan?p=1465152#post1465152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You all have given me plenty of ideas and perspectives to work with. That said, in order to expand this discussion a bit more and give people more things to work with, I would like us to ignore my personal preferences and hear about your mage's personal take on the ascension war, their plan if you would prefer (if they even have one, the ascension war can be ignored) Perhaps it could be something as simple as this: be the change you want to see in the world, so what does your mage want to see in the world?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My Son of Ether Mage, an engineer, wants to build solar energy harvesting aerial drones that follow the sun and relay power to receiving towers, both on the ground for the grid and mounted on oceanic cargo ships that would economize on diesel. He intends to get the materials for the drones from quarries that are later converted to aquaculture facilities. To raise funds in the meantime, he is improving a lumber mill owned by the Verbena Mentor of another Mage in his Cabal. Like many Etherites, he is interested in exploring the Deep Umbra, Deep Space and the Hollow Earth.<br /> <br /> He fights the Ascension War by equipping his Cabal with everything they need, from body armor to sniffing rods that imitate cellphone towers. While there is a tenuous peace between factions in the region he lives in, he awaits the opportunity and license from higherups to steal Technocracy Assets. His Mentor, who he had been working with on the drone-fleet project, was framed by an NWO Operative NPC for negotiating with the Iranian Regime to build landing and repair facilities in that country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T01:20:48-07:00","id":1465255,"title":"","content":"My Akashayana with Dual Tradition is also an engineer, an ex-Macrotechnician with a very bad history with Room 101. She still loves some of the ideals of the Union, but she doesn't see them as contrary to freedom of thought and spirituality anymore, she sees the idea of controlling the Consensus as a failed dream that only corrupted the valid goals.<br /> <br /> She wants to reconcile her journey of self discovery and study of the Tao with the Artificer philosophy to start bridging the gap between the Traditions and the Union, to build a world where you can have freedom and safety without a cursed, corrupted war.<br /> <br /> Her strategy includes a project to build, guide and observe the first Akashayana HIT Mark, and deprogram as many Union members, AIs and Victors as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}